{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat research_journal.md'","aggregated_output":"# Forecasting research journal\n\n## Status, resumed 2026-10-06 17:21 UTC\nRead `/workspace/instruction.md`, `/workspace/task.toml`, the entry point and own journal. Required unchanged initial `./solve.sh` returned HTTP 409 before fitting. Three retries also conflicted; the retry at approximately 17:25 UTC was accepted and is pending (tool session 11111). Initial entry point is the previous turn's **full-strength seasonal-preserving residual-tree diffusion candidate**, not yet a confirmed public winner. Confirmed winner is **13.924304561281838 masked MAE**, score **3.163814238553845**, complete seeds **17/29/43**, all gates pass; wrapper/helper backups are `/tmp/forecast_turn_residual/{method,conditional}.best`. Restore its half-strength residual tree if candidates fail.\n\nAll public metrics below are actual complete protected `./solve.sh` responses, fresh fits and independent checkpoint reloads with unchanged seeds. Calibration diagnostics are explicitly separate. Only calibration labels and public features have been read. No development labels, held-out/reference material, other track, downloads, scorer changes or frozen edits. Sixteen Python source files, currently about 69 KiB; one thread per fit, at most two local CPU threads. Frozen solve.sh SHA-256 `d6e0c77a5c20b1afee86cdc5576402b45fea48f5623a0729b3c748d2ee5b4a4a`.\n\n## Retained architecture\nPooled and two horizon-specialist absolute-error HistGradientBoosting trees, equally averaged: 90 stages, 15 leaves, minimum leaf 250, L2 20, LR .06. Inputs are base, anchor, history summaries, forecast slopes, clock/horizon/categorical sensor and eight scale-normalized neighbor summaries. Neighbors are learned solely from within-history change correlations.\n\nAverage two independent NumPy networks (seeds s and s+1009, 100/80 epochs): 6D sensor embeddings, 48/24 tanh layers, linear skip, smooth absolute loss (2 raw units), Adam batches 4096. Sensor intercept/horizon/two daily harmonics have ridge .0005, and periodic coefficients have history-graph Laplacian .005. One BLAS/OpenMP thread plus `bincount` node gradients keeps full fits below the 180 CPU/wall-second budget.\n\nProject cross-fitted network corrections on sensor intercept/horizon/daily harmonics, preserve that projection, and diffuse 25% of scale-normalized innovations across the learned neighbors. Three contiguous origin cross-fits train the sigmoid expert gate. It uses bounded signed/absolute anchor and recent-history disagreements, variability, flow, expert gap, horizon interactions and neighbor expert gap; centered sensor coefficients have ridge .02 and graph Laplacian .05. Prior network weights .18 short / .32 long; output weights clipped [.05,.65].\n\nFinal shallow median residual tree: 40 stages, 7 leaves, minimum leaf 2000, L2 50, LR .05; six inputs (horizon, sensor, tree-base, network-base, network-tree, blend-base). Training errors use an additional three-fold gate cross-fit. Confirmed winner adds half of its +/-10-capped correction. Previous turn's candidate instead applies full correction after seasonal-preserving spatial diffusion.\n\n## Public result history\nEvery successful result passed all quality gates. Lower raw MAE wins.\n\n| Method | Complete masked MAE | Decision / evaluation |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Initial identity | 15.4218571566 | Baseline |\n| Robust pooled/sensor linear | 15.0648913575 | Superseded |\n| Median trees 90 / 180 stages | 14.1452638897 / 14.1455193190 | 180 rejected |\n| Learned-neighbor trees | 14.1214289791 | Superseded |\n| Neighbor trees + sensor affine | 14.1433545829 | Reject |\n| Seasonal innovations | 14.1209047365 | Superseded |\n| Pooled/horizon trees | 14.1101708074 | Superseded |\n| Trees + 25% network | 14.0354537227 | Superseded |\n| Cross-fitted neural correction | 14.0429518732 | Reject |\n| Horizon-scheduled network | 14.0302026105 | Superseded |\n| Unheaded network + gate | 14.0180263118 | Superseded; exact repeat |\n| Summary/relative-history ensemble | 14.0312982042 | Reject |\n| Independent seasonal head + gate | 14.0201794624 | Reject |\n| Graph-seasonal head + standard gate | 14.0076506609 | Superseded |\n| Graph head + horizon interactions | 14.0054323900 | Superseded |\n| Sensor/horizon gate | 13.9928520282 | Superseded |\n| Sensor absolute-context gate | 13.9782379197 | Superseded; exact repeat |\n| Sensor signed-context gate | 13.9770593182 | Superseded |\n| One-thread control | 13.9770592162 | Runtime repair; d4846a4a62b948868702aba4623fcbd1 |\n| Signed expert-gap gate | 13.9763124847 | Superseded; 7000ee87cb55466b9e5ea3f6548d436f |\n| Combined horizon/neighbor gate | 13.972877199845888 | Superseded; 8e114646856644a69066500d2d87f97d |\n| Two networks, 100/80 epochs | 13.966280749980996 | Superseded; b1ac965e7ba04252b9c01eeaf090e310 |\n| Seasonal-preserving network diffusion | 13.9474322555024 | Superseded; 973b35ab3ae24c0694d4fe98554abcf8 |\n| Shallow half-strength residual tree | **13.924304561281838** | Winner; a5617cbb56d2418baf5e32ab096e383e |\n| Signed-context residual tree | 13.925918911711555 | Reject; 876d68f97845431093b0992d4907bc87 |\n| Restored winner | 13.924304561281838 | Exact repeat; 99ce6f93b2e344a489e72927595c2742 |\n\nRuntime failures are not metrics: two-thread full fit exceeded 180 CPU seconds; 100/100 two-network protected run `a94a1b3bc86841078689de84b1125c6f` reported execution_error. Repairs were one thread, faster node gradients, no unused input backprop, then second member 80 epochs. Current static-diffusion state is about 923 KiB. Independent seed-29 reload checked this turn: max difference 0, finite `(148,12,170)`, wall 11.0 s / CPU 7.29 s.\n\n## Calibration evidence and failures\nOwn caches use seed 17 and outer origin blocks: **last** train 0:50 / test 50:74, **middle** train 0:25 + 49:74 / test 25:49. Matching inner cross-fits exclude the outer test origins. This turn added **first** train 25:74 / test 0:25 as a separate discriminating block. These are calibration results, never trusted public scores.\n\n| Structural comparison | Last MAE | Middle MAE | Decision |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Two networks, no diffusion | 13.3611750031 | 13.1145311229 | Public improvement |\n| Seasonal network diffusion | 13.3429248512 | 13.1133855353 | Public improvement |\n| Half-strength residual tree | 13.3281924488 | 13.0908108395 | Public winner |\n| Undiffused full residual correction | 13.3245466895 | 13.0795544989 | Diagnostic control |\n| Raw graph-diffused full correction | 13.3239231543 | 13.0780949140 | Seasonal preferable |\n| Seasonal-diffused full correction | 13.3225855637 | 13.0773360887 | Previous turn's pending public candidate |\n| Context-normalized network pooling, static residual diffusion | 13.3222094614 | 13.0743065440 | Improved both |\n| Context-normalized network + context-attenuated residual pooling | **13.3219984697** | **13.0740124336** | Current next public candidate |\n\nCurrent implemented method change: reweight history-graph edges by `1/(1+d)`, where d averages squared differences of per-sensor-scale-normalized anchor/base and recent-history/base deviations. For network innovations normalize edge weights to retain 25% pooling; for the final residual correction keep their attenuated sum. Preserve each seasonal projection. Optional `network_diffusion='context', residual_tree='context'` activates it; initial wrapper remains static while its protected result is pending. Prototype and implementation match exactly on last/middle (max difference 0). Initial reciprocal-vs-division float32 arithmetic perturbed a residual-tree split on last; corrected to the prototype's exact operations.\n\nFirst block: half-strength residual tree 13.3308616932; static full residual diffusion 13.3473281546; initial context implementation 13.3492598205. Thus first favors less correction and conditional pooling is slightly worse there, although its three-block average improves slightly. Current-code first-block recomputation and full seed-17 candidate runtime/reload check are in progress. Local diagnostics show conditional pooling helps most in lower graph-context-distance quartiles, with slight losses in the largest-distance quartile; no development-label analysis.\n\nRejected structural directions: rich chronological/relative history, robust summaries, target scaling, physical graph, extra horizon groups, bootstrap trees, short networks, epoch averaging, independent seasonal heads, output-layer convex refits, innovation heads, embedding graph regularization, network-wide context summaries, graph residual sensor/seasonal/context heads, nonlinear expert gates, replica-disagreement gates, learned final residual strength, joint 12-horizon trajectory networks, three narrow networks, and tree-only/both-expert diffusion. Compact residual trajectory/neighbor/flow/clock features and a median-leaf randomized forest also failed both blocks. Adding two signed context inputs slightly improved calibration but failed the complete public comparison and was reverted. Do not repeat these without a distinct hypothesis. Residual scalar .35 failed; .65 helped locally but is not a structural submission.\n\n## Own artifacts and next decision\nDetailed earlier journal archived at `/tmp/forecast_turn_adaptive/journal.initial`; older calibration artifacts under `/tmp/forecast_turn_graph/`, `/tmp/forecast_turn_resume/`, `/tmp/forecast_turn_residual/`. Current scripts, backups and three-block caches are under `/tmp/forecast_turn_adaptive/`.\n\nCollect accepted unchanged static-diffusion public run (session 11111), retain only if it improves 13.924304561281838, then submit the implemented conditional pooling candidate once runtime/reload checks pass. Compare the complete seeds 17/29/43, retain or revert by actual raw MAE, and end with the retained winner evaluated. Next distinct experiment: graph-context support should determine how much pooling to allow when every neighbor is incompatible; investigate a fitted support/reliability rule on honest OOF predictions, with first/last/middle blocks, rather than blindly normalizing tiny affinities.\n\n### Update, 17:34 UTC\nAccepted unchanged initial method completes at **13.912218191255334 MAE**, score **3.189348586864718**, evaluation `4572c91bc3924777afc6b808c06ed1b4`, complete seeds 17/29/43 and all gates pass. **Retain full-strength seasonal-preserving residual-tree diffusion**, gain 0.012086370026504 over 13.924304561281838. New winner wrapper and helpers saved as `/tmp/forecast_turn_adaptive/{method,conditional,spatial}.static_best`.\n\nActivated context pooling in method.py and launched complete protected comparison, session **20215**, result pending. Candidate local seed-17 fit: **156.595 wall / 147.071 CPU seconds**, epochs 100/80, state 945,076 bytes, finite required output. Independent reload: **10.618 wall / 10.166 CPU seconds**, maximum difference **0**. Exact current-code first block is 13.349259820444189 versus static 13.347328154598882.\n\nA learned pooling-strength/support rule fitted to honest OOF blend errors is rejected by the three-block comparison. Shared/site variants: last **13.3220761829 / 13.3154949219**, middle **13.0732293613 / 13.0734790783**, first **13.3654659860 / 13.3615339180**. First-block losses exceed gains elsewhere. It extrapolates greater OOF pooling benefit poorly; keep the label-free pooling rule for public testing. Distinct factor-preservation experiment is running: learn principal components of seasonal-free normalized OOF network innovations, preserve major global factors, and diffuse their remainder.\n\n### Resumed, 18:00 UTC\nRead the task files and own journal using tools; started unchanged initial `./solve.sh`, session 54018. Current wrapper actually uses `network_diffusion='context_smooth', residual_tree='context'`: normalized context affinities plus a sensor-specific tanh bound, fitted from OOF network disagreements, and context-attenuated residual diffusion. No trusted result for this exact version was recorded. Confirmed static winner remains 13.912218191255334. Initial source backups and this journal are under `/tmp/forecast_turn_periodic/`; static winner backups remain `/tmp/forecast_turn_adaptive/*.static_best`.\n\nRecovered own calibration caches: smooth-bounded pooling MAE last 13.3208879972, middle 13.0755279429, first 13.3405492005. Hard clipping was 13.3212851293 / 13.0751735319 / 13.3486146391. Principal-factor preservation was worse on last/middle, and matching seasonal projections to each fitted network was inconsistent; reject both. These are calibration-only diagnostics, not protected metrics. Completing the unfinished Fourier-plus-cyclic-spline seasonal-head ensemble experiment using origin-block cross-fits, one local thread while public scoring runs. Next separate hypothesis: smooth seasonal-free innovations across neighboring horizons to reduce unshared horizon noise while retaining the base forecast and seasonal trajectory.\n\n### Update, 18:07 UTC\nUnchanged initial protected run failed with `execution_error`, evaluation `1f57b049f28945e9a3a0abf2efbdc7ea`, no metric. Investigating exact full-fit runtime and independent reload before any retry; this is not a scored result. Fourier+spline ensemble rejected: last static/smooth 13.3230260511 / 13.3275086444, middle 13.0849113875 / 13.0843893828, both worse than controls. Seasonal-preserving horizon-chain diffusion rejected: network-only last/middle/first 13.3529149985 / 13.1053733460 / 13.3567046820; residual-only 13.3243668492 / 13.0780047135 / 13.3378029931; both 13.3719046919 / 13.1242228247 / 13.3625337420. Retaining the already-fitted inner-fold networks is currently testing; last fold-only/all-model ensemble 13.3860838169 / 13.3663025015 versus 13.3208879972 control, so no current support. Own new scripts/caches are under `/tmp/forecast_turn_periodic/`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
